  "hints": [
    "Look at a single position. What decides how high the water above it can rise?",
    "Water above `i` is `min(tallest bar on the left, tallest bar on the right) - heights[i]`. With two pointers at both ends and running maxima `left_max` and `right_max`, always move the side with the smaller maximum: that side's water level is already known.",
    "Parallel example: a valley between two hills can only fill up to the height of the lower hill; any extra water spills over that side."
  ],
